+||| The order a compile-time tree splits the arguments in. The tree a
+||| definition is evaluated by takes them from the left. The tree an erased
+||| function's coverage is checked by takes first the arguments a run would
+||| keep, from the left, then the erased ones from the right: a later
+||| argument's type names the earlier ones, so the later determine the
+||| earlier (an index is bound before the argument whose type it is in, and
+||| a case block's environment before its scrutinee). Where that tree split
+||| an index first, it ended at every value of the index no clause has with
+||| the arguments that determine it unsplit, a case the coverage check
+||| cannot refute without splitting them, and it walked the rest of the
+||| tree again for every constructor such a default stands for.
